{"chunk_id": "ba1ca4b9b4e2", "text": "This section concludes the story of Sakuntala and King Dushmanta and then turns toward the great genealogies that lead to the Bharata dynasty. Sakuntala defends the legitimacy of her son and extols truth as the highest virtue, greater even than sacrifices or lineage. After she departs, a divine voice confirms that the child is truly Dushmanta\u2019s son and commands the king to accept him. The king publicly acknowledges the boy, names him Bharata, and installs him as heir; Bharata later becomes a world\u2011conquering emperor whose lineage gives its name to the Bharata race. The narrative then shifts into mythic history, recounting the descent from Daksha, Manu, and Pururavas through Nahusha and Yayati, setting up the ancestral lines that will eventually produce the great royal houses central to the epic.\nSakuntala\u2019s son is divinely affirmed as Dushmanta\u2019s heir, becoming Bharata; the narrative then shifts into the sacred genealogy leading to Yayati and Puru.\nThemes: truth and dharma, legitimacy of lineage, divine validation, royal genealogy, father\u2013son duty", "vector": [0.011133224703371525, -0.0009582145721651614, -4.561691093840636e-05, -0.011239508166909218, -0.030450299382209778, 0.01923736184835434, -0.020074347034096718, 0.0016731390496715903, -0.018413662910461426, -0.0035040429793298244, 0.003945785108953714, 0.002205388154834509, 0.007380079012364149, 0.025986380875110626, -0.0025043112691491842, -0.00023996882373467088, 0.040759824216365814, -0.03316053748130798, 0.019197504967451096, -0.0224923025816679, -0.0019014830468222499, -0.01243520062416792, 0.0024960078299045563, 0.021376322954893112, -0.01903807930648327, 0.02723521552979946, 0.015145436860620975, -0.030716009438037872, 0.011379006318747997, -0.01696554571390152, -0.010488878935575485, 0.00037946627708151937, 0.007772000506520271, -0.008416346274316311, -0.01769624650478363, -0.0041915662586688995, -0.018719227984547615, -0.01436159387230873